Package: grillr
Title: Parse and Extract Data from Excel Templates Using Functional Tags
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("First", "Last", email = "first.last@example.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides a workflow for extracting structured data from Excel
    files that follow a fixed template layout.  The analyst creates a *guide*
    workbook — a copy of the template where every cell carries a parsable tag
    string encoding functional dimensions (e.g. metric, scenario, tenor).
    grillr reads the guide to build a cell-to-dimensions mapping, applies that
    mapping to the actual data file, and returns a long tidy dataset where each
    observation is fully labelled.  An optional YAML sidecar file holds
    template-level metadata such as reference date or reporting entity.
